# Phase:        pre
# Target:       symmetric/src/hax_reshaped.rs, symmetric/src/sponge.rs
# Hunks:        4
# Class:        equiv-rewrite
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 23 (aeneas rejects a return or a
#               continue that leaves a nested loop).
# Cost:         none in a normal build: only the selection is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant,
#               `Pad10Sponge::hash_iter` calls the reshaped body, which a
#               differential test equates with the original.
# Upstreamable: no: the original is the clearer code; aeneas support for
#               leaving a nested loop makes the patch unnecessary.
# Drop when:    aeneas translates a `return` out of a nested loop.
# Test:         test p3-symmetric --lib hax_reshaped
# Mutation:     the reshaped body overwrites the first capacity element with
#               d(0) instead of applying the derangement to it, so it disagrees
#               on every non-empty multiple of the rate.
#
# The original returns from inside its block loop, and peeks to learn whether a full block is the last one.
# The reshaped body runs one loop over the input.
# It delays the permutation of a full block until the next element arrives, which is what the peek decides.
# It pads and permutes at the same points as the original.
#
